      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I recommend consulting a pediatrician as soon as possible to get a proper diagnosis. While it's possible that the red spots are related to a heat rash, the fact that the fever is present and they didn't respond to the cold surface test suggests there might be a more underlying condition that needs attention. Infantility red spots, also known as Hungry Baby spots, are a common condition in young children but may need medical evaluation. Waiting until morning may not be appropriate.",
